{"name":"Cape Cod Blue","hex":"#91a2a6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece or point of land, extending beyond the adjacent coast into a sea or lake; a promontory; a headland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sleeveless garment or part of a garment, hanging from the neck over the back, arms, and shoulders.","A superhero."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cape"},{"term":"cod","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Cocama."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various types of sea fish or the meat from said fish.","A sea fish of the family Gadidae which are sold as \"cod\", as haddock (Melanogrammus aeglefinus), and whiting (usually Merlangius merlangus).\n A sea fish of the genus Gadus, inclusive of Atlantic cod (Gadus morhua), Pacific cod (Gadus macrocephalus), and Greenland cod (Gadus ogac or Gadus macrocephalus ogac).\n An Atlantic cod (Gadus morhua)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cod"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cape Cod","blocks":[{"text":"Cape Cod is a peninsula extending into the Atlantic Ocean from the southeastern corner of Massachusetts, in the northeastern United States. Its historic, maritime character and ample beaches attract heavy tourism during the summer months. The name Cape Cod, coined in 1602 by Bartholomew Gosnold, is the ninth-oldest English place-name in the U.S."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/White_Crest_Beach_Wellfleet.jpg/330px-White_Crest_Beach_Wellfleet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape_Cod","wikidata":"Q49152"},{"title":"Cape","blocks":[{"text":"A cape is a clothing accessory or a sleeveless outer garment of any length that hangs loosely and connects either at the neck or shoulders. They usually cover the back, shoulders, and arms. They come in a variety of styles and have been used throughout history for many different reasons."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape","wikidata":"Q1034198"},{"title":"Cod","blocks":[{"text":"Cod is the common name for the demersal fish genus Gadus, belonging to the family Gadidae. Cod is also used as part of the common name for several other fish species, and one species that belongs to genus Gadus is not commonly called cod."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Gadus_morhua_Cod-2b-Atlanterhavsparken-Norway.JPG/330px-Gadus_morhua_Cod-2b-Atlanterhavsparken-Norway.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cod","wikidata":"Q13194939"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&